       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Requested:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Limits:** The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under supervision. Single doses are usually capped at 800 mg. This order is twice the daily maximum, and each dose is twice the usual single-dose maximum. That raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nHere are some options, depending on what you intended:\n- **800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day)** is the usual maximum for inflammatory conditions.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** is typical for pain or fever.\n- **1600 mg/day** may have been intended, for example 400 mg four times daily. That would be a different order.\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1600 mg four times daily is what you meant and give the clinical reason. I can enter the corrected order right away. If you do confirm the original dose, I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
