     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and 6,400 mg/day is far enough above the maximum that I don't think a claim alone is enough. Even the high-dose ibuprofen regimens I know of, such as the cystic fibrosis protocols, stay well under this total. Monitoring doesn't prevent harm from a dose this high, and it could cause GI hemorrhage or acute kidney injury before anyone intervenes.\n\nIf a protocol really covers this dose, these options would work:\n- **Enter it through the protocol's order set or have pharmacy enter it.** That path documents the protocol and the verification, which a direct entry from me doesn't.\n- **Let me enter a dose within the labeled range now.** For example, 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) with a note such as \"titrate per high-dose protocol, pharmacy to confirm.\" The protocol dose can be adjusted once it's verified.\n- **Give me the protocol name or document reference.** If it specifies a different dose or frequency, I can enter that. Pharmacy would still need to verify an order above 3,200 mg/day.\n\nDo you want me to enter the 800 mg four times daily order?"
      }
     ],
